# Every `.env` variant, not two named ones. `.env` and `.env.local` were listed individually, which
# quietly left `.env.production`, `.env.hosted` and anything else a deploy invents publishable — in a
# public repository, by whoever creates the file next and does not think to check.
.env*
!.env.example
.temporal/
.meridian/*
!.meridian/.gitkeep
.playwright-browsers/
test-results/
playwright-report/
coverage/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
.DS_Store

# The assignment brief and the customer SOP it references are Meridian's material, not this
# repository's, and this repository is public. They stay on disk — `docs/PRD.md` cites the brief as
# its baseline and `verify-tree` still allows it to sit at the root — but they are not published.
*.docx
